-- title:
--   Adelic box of a conjugated lattice equals gwidehatΛ g⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$, and let $g$ be a unit of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ denotes `FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ`. For a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $M \subseteq D$, [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox M`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) is the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z \otimes a$ with $z \in M$ and $a$ a finite adele all of whose components $a_v$ lie in the valuation ring $v$-$\mathrm{adicCompletionIntegers}$, for every $v$ in the height one spectrum of $\mathbb{Z}$; and [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ obtained by pulling back, along the inclusion $d \mapsto d \otimes 1$, the image of [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) under the additive endomorphism $x \mapsto g x g^{-1}$ (left multiplication by $g$ followed by right multiplication by $g^{-1}$). The assertion is that the adelic box of this conjugated lattice coincides with the image of the adelic box of $\Lambda$ under the same endomorphism $x \mapsto g x g^{-1}$, the two sides being equal as additive subgroups of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$.
--
--   This is the two-sided local–global statement for lattices: the $\widehat{\mathbb{Z}}$-lattice $g\widehat\Lambda g^{-1}$ is recovered as the adelic box of its global points $D \cap g\widehat\Lambda g^{-1}$, the two-sided companion of the identity $\widehat{D \cap g\widehat\Lambda} = g\widehat\Lambda$. It is used throughout the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower arguments, where $\Lambda$ is an order in a quaternion algebra and [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) is the order attached to an idele $g$, to identify the orders arising from Hecke correspondences as Eichler orders.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_finiteAdeleBox_conjByFiniteIdele.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped TensorProduct Pointwise
open IsDedekindDomain NumberField

theorem Submodule.finiteAdeleBox_conjByFiniteIdele
    {D : Type*} [Ring D] [Algebra ℚ D] (Λ : Submodule ℤ D) (hfg : Λ.FG)
    (hspan : Submodule.span ℚ (Λ : Set D) = ⊤) (g : (D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)ˣ) :
    Submodule.finiteAdeleBox (Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ g)
      = (Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ).map
          ((AddMonoidHom.mulRight ((g⁻¹ : (D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)ˣ) : D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)).comp
            (AddMonoidHom.mulLeft (g : D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ))) := by sorry
